    {
      "id": 793,
      "q": 2,
      "section": "Physics",
      "text": "A Carnot engine operates between two reservoirs at temperatures 500 K and 300 K. What is the efficiency of the engine?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "0.2",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "0.4",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "0.6",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "0.8",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "The efficiency of a Carnot engine is given by the equation eta = 1 - (T2/T1), where T1 and T2 are the temperatures of the two reservoirs. For the given temperatures, eta = 1 - (300/500) = 1 - 0.6 = 0.4."
    },
