    {
      "id": 814,
      "q": 4,
      "section": "Chemistry",
      "text": "What is the molecular formula of the compound with the empirical formula CH2O and a molecular weight of 120 g/mol?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "C2H4O2",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "C3H6O3",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "C4H8O4",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "C5H10O5",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "The empirical formula is CH2O, and its molecular weight is 30 g/mol. To find the molecular formula, we need to multiply the empirical formula by a factor that will give us the molecular weight of 120 g/mol. The factor is 120 / 30 = 4. So, the molecular formula is (CH2O) * 4 = C4H8O4 * (3/4) = C3H6O3."
    },
    {
      "id": 789,
      "q": 5,
      "section": "Mathematics",
      "text": "If the equation x^2 + 2x + 1 = 0 has two equal roots, what is the value of the discriminant?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "0",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "1",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "2",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "4",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "The discriminant of a quadratic equation ax^2 + bx + c = 0 is given by b^2 - 4ac. For the given equation x^2 + 2x + 1 = 0, a = 1, b = 2, and c = 1. The discriminant is 2^2 - 4*1*1 = 0."
    },
