      "section": "Physics",
      "text": "A block of mass 5 kg is moving with a velocity of 2 m/s. What is the magnitude of its momentum?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "5 kg m/s",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "10 kg m/s",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "15 kg m/s",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "20 kg m/s",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "The momentum of an object is given by the product of its mass and velocity. So, the magnitude of the momentum is p = mv = 5 kg * 2 m/s = 10 kg m/s."
