    {
      "id": 815,
      "q": 12,
      "section": "Mathematics",
      "text": "If the function f(x) = x^3 - 2x^2 - 5x + 1 is given, what is the value of f(-1)?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "1",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "3",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "5",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "7",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "solution": "To find the value of f(-1), we substitute x = -1 into the function: f(-1) = (-1)^3 - 2(-1)^2 - 5(-1) + 1 = -1 - 2 + 5 + 1 = 3."
    },
