      "id": 810,
      "q": 14,
      "section": "Physics",
      "text": "An electron in the ground state of a hydrogen atom has an energy of -13.6 eV. What is the energy of the electron in the first excited state?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "-3.4 eV",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "-6.8 eV",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "-10.2 eV",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "-13.6 eV",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "The energy of the electron in the nth state of a hydrogen atom is given by En = -13.6 eV / n^2. For the first excited state, n = 2. So, E2 = -13.6 eV / 2^2 = -13.6 eV / 4 = -3.4 eV."
    },
